ing a  private detective I'm not a big fan of  um they sometimes start parallel  investigations they talk to other  witnesses that you've already talked to  and that can kind of complicate and  interfere with the investigation I was  never a fan of that when I was working  on the inside as an investigator me and  the prosecutors would be working towards  things and when someone else is out  there talking to witnesses that we've  already talked to or you know that's  that's that was problematic to me  Brian it's interesting because when we  discussed this you said that having an  outside investigator in a case like this  is kind of like a dual-edged sword why  do you say that it's a dual-edged sword  in the sense that as much as you're  helping the case you could be hurting  yourself as well depending on how you  wield that sword now Bobby's correct  that's kind of the concept of too many  chefs in the kitchen everything gets  burned if you have an investigator  running a parallel or intercepting an  investigation they can kind of stumble  on each other but depending on how this  investigator goes about they could  actually reach out to witnesses that the  law enforcement never knew about I know  in New York especially in other states  depending on the relationship between  the police and the community sometimes  people will speak to the investigator of  the family because they're sympathetic  to the family needs more so or quicker  than they would to the police but if  they work in conjunction or together it  could actually be helpful yeah and we  know that Mr Gonzalez has identified who  the private investigator is but that it  seems to be someone whose former law  enforcement Terry I get the frustration  I completely do but just frustration  equal legal liability because part of  the things that I wonder is do you think  that any of the parents are going to end  up suing the authorities for the way  they're handling this case well I hope  that doesn't happen and i